4️⃣ Monitoring Blind Spot → Delayed Detection


“In one case, our dashboards looked healthy from an infrastructure perspective — CPU, memory, and disk were all green. However, users started complaining 
about slow responses and failed requests.

The problem was that the issue went unnoticed for several minutes because support tickets arrived before alerts, which is never a good sign.

On investigation, we realized our alerts were based almost entirely on infrastructure metrics and not on user-facing signals.

We addressed this by adding alerts on latency, error rate, and request success, aligned directly with our SLIs.

After that change, similar issues were detected much earlier, often before users noticed.

The major learning was shifting from infra-based monitoring to SLI-driven alerting, which significantly reduced detection time.”
